    {
      "id": "ea6da0f09967-q1",
      "number": 1,
      "question": "The sides PQ and PR of &Delta;PQR are produced to points S and T, respectively. The bisectors of &ang;SQR and &ang;TRQ meet at point U. If &ang;QUR = 69&deg;, then the measure of &ang;P is:",
      "questionHtml": "The sides PQ and PR of&nbsp;&Delta;PQR are produced to points S and T, respectively. The bisectors of&nbsp;&ang;SQR and&nbsp;&ang;TRQ meet at point U. If&nbsp;&ang;QUR = 69&deg;, then the measure of&nbsp;&ang;P is:",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "69&deg;",
          "html": "69&deg;"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "21&deg;",
          "html": "21&deg;"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "42&deg;",
          "html": "42&deg;"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "31&deg;",
          "html": "31&deg;"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/shortcut-trick-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Shortcut Trick</u></span></strong></span></p>\n\n<p>Given,&nbsp;<span style=\"\">&ang;QUR = 69&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p>If t<span style=\"\">he bisectors of&nbsp;&ang;SQR and&nbsp;&ang;TRQ meet at point U</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&ang;QUR = 90&deg; -&nbsp;&ang;P/2</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr; &ang;QUR = (180&deg; -&nbsp;&ang;P)/2</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;69&deg; =&nbsp;(180&deg; -&nbsp;&ang;P)/2</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;180&deg; -&nbsp;&ang;P </span>= 2&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;69&deg; = 138&deg;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;</span>&ang;P =&nbsp;180&deg; - 138&deg; = 42&deg;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&there4; The measure of&nbsp;&ang;P is&nbsp;42&deg;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/alternate-methord-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Alternate Method</u></span></strong></span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&ang;QUR = 69&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"\">Concept used:</span></strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">The sum of all angles on a straight line is 180&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">The sum of all angles of a triangle is 180&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"\">Calculation:</span></strong></p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Madhuri_SSC_22.06.2022_D15.png\" style=\"height: 194px; width: 197px;\" /></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&ang;PQR +&nbsp;&ang;RQS = 180&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;&ang;RQS = 180&deg; -&nbsp;&ang;PQR</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;&ang;RQS/2 = (180&deg; -&nbsp;&ang;PQR)/2</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;&ang;RQS/2 = 90&deg; -&nbsp;&ang;PQR/2</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;&ang;RQU =&nbsp;90&deg; -&nbsp;&ang;PQR/2&nbsp; [∵ QU is the bisector of &ang;RQS]</span></p>\n\n<p>Similarly,&nbsp;&ang;QRU =&nbsp;<span style=\"\">90&deg; -&nbsp;&ang;PRQ/2</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">In&nbsp;&Delta;QUR,&nbsp;&ang;RQU +&nbsp;&ang;QRU +&nbsp;&ang;QUR = 180&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;</span>[<span style=\"\">90&deg; -&nbsp;&ang;PQR/2</span>] + [<span style=\"\">90&deg; -&nbsp;&ang;PRQ/2</span>] + 69&deg;&nbsp;= 180&deg;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;</span>180&deg; - [<span style=\"\">&ang;PQR/2 +&nbsp;&ang;PRQ/2</span>] +&nbsp;<span style=\"\">69&deg;&nbsp;= 180&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;180&deg; - [(&ang;PQR&nbsp;+&nbsp;&ang;PRQ)/2</span><span style=\"\">] +&nbsp;</span><span style=\"\">69&deg;&nbsp;= 180&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;180&deg; - [(180&deg; - &ang;P)/2] +&nbsp;69&deg;&nbsp;= 180&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;[(180&deg; - &ang;P)/2] = 69&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;180&deg; - &ang;P = 2&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;69&deg; = 138&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;&ang;P =&nbsp;180&deg; - 138&deg; = 42&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"\">&there4; The measure of&nbsp;&ang;P is&nbsp;42&deg;</span></strong></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/shortcut-trick-image.png",
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/alternate-methord-image.png",
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/06/F1_Madhuri_SSC_22.06.2022_D15.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
